Package: confd
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Description: Go-based NETCONF server backed by sysrepo
 confd is a NETCONF server that uses sysrepo as its datastore backend.
 It provides RFC 6241 compliant NETCONF operations (get, get-config,
 edit-config, lock, unlock, commit, discard-changes, validate, get-schema)
 over SSH, with an interactive CLI shell for management.
 .
 Features:
  * goyang-based YANG schema cache with auto-discovery from sysrepo
  * Telekom sysrepo-plugins hosting (dlopen-based, crash-safe)
  * Interactive CLI shell with YAML config rendering (show running/startup)
  * Auto-connect to local server at launch
  * CIDR notation for IP addresses in YAML output

Package: confd-dev
Architecture: all
Depends: confd (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Development files for confd
 Headers and development files for confd plugin development.
